Addresses INV-guzuj. go.py's bare-identifier call arm tried a local symbol,
the resolver, the INV-fahub deferral and the dot-import placeholder. A name
that fell through all of them emitted no calls edge: an unknown name, or a
same-package helper the resolver withholds as ambiguous. It now emits the
`external` placeholder via make_unresolved_edge, as every other analyzer
does and Python has since INV-foluz.

A name bound anywhere in the enclosing top-level declaration (a closure, a
function-typed parameter, a range variable, a select receive, a type-switch
alias) stays unemitted, per INV-foluz's rule. The dot-import arm, which
attributed any bare name to the first dot-imported package, applies the
same refusal. The bound set is computed once per declaration.

Read back against source on dev 62a70cd1b3 (pinned worktree) vs this
branch: alertmanager +124 call edges, beads +379, every one an external
placeholder. All 16 sampled sites are real calls: same-package test helpers
(New(...), newTestStore(...), runGit(...)) withheld by the ambiguity
guard. One edge is removed, correctly: alertmanager send_test.go:65 calls a
local closure `timerange` that the dot-import arm had attributed to the
dot-imported with_api_v2 package.

